{'_client': <twikit.client.client.Client object at 0x000001E534E2AE40>, '_data': {'__typename': 'Tweet', 'rest_id': '1884664717630988357', 'core': {'user_results': {'result': {'__typename': 'User', 'id': 'VXNlcjoxMDk5NjUzODY2MzQwMjA4NjQ1', 'rest_id': '1099653866340208645', 'affiliates_highlighted_label': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': False, 'can_media_tag': True, 'created_at': 'Sun Feb 24 12:54:47 +0000 2019', 'default_profile': True, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': 'Ex-Army Infantry Paratrooper, Combat Vet, A&P Mechanic. Servant of His Majesty, Jesus Christ, through Our Lady of the Forsaken (La Virgen de los Desamparados)', 'entities': {'description': {'urls': []}, 'url': {'urls': [{'display_url': 'RadioFreeCatholic.com', 'expanded_url': 'http://www.RadioFreeCatholic.com', 'url': 'https://t.co/wmuUk1AZuI', 'indices': [0, 23]}]}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 23664, 'followers_count': 836, 'friends_count': 911, 'has_custom_timelines': True, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 6, 'location': 'Montana, USA', 'media_count': 1042, 'name': 'Caleb the Mechanic at Radio Free Catholic', 'normal_followers_count': 836, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': ['1933956733271241021'], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_banner_url': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1099653866340208645/1738165346', 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1886768696343060480/9IYNa4MW_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'CalebMechanic', 'statuses_count': 13637, 'translator_type': 'none', 'url': 'https://t.co/wmuUk1AZuI', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}, 'professional': {'rest_id': '1810528490812489758', 'professional_type': 'Creator', 'category': [{'id': 934, 'name': 'Social Media Influencer', 'icon_name': 'IconBriefcaseStroke'}]}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1884664717630988357'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1738177658000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '3260', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="https://mobile.twitter.com" rel="nofollow">Twitter Web App</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4ODQ2NjQ3MTczODc3MTg2NTc=', 'text': 'I have an analogy for you. Please bear with me.\n\nA woman wants to have a baby, but she\'s afraid of the pain and effort involved in delivery. Scientists and engineers decide that the way to alleviate the pain and risks involved in childbirth is to develop a machine that can deliver the baby by going in and getting the child when the first labor pangs hit.\n\nGovernment and medical associations buy in, and the project is funded.\n\nThe machine, designed to be compact enough to fit, is deployed into the womb and retrieves the child. In the process, the baby is maimed and killed and the mother suffers injury that risks sterilizing her.\n\nThe family sues. The doctors pay. Governments and medical associations fund R&D to improve the design. Corporations go back to work. Insurance companies volunteer to cover the doctors and the patients.\n\nThey go back to the drawing board and develop a new machine. This time it is designed to expand around the child and safely retrieve the baby. When the labor pangs hit, the machine is deployed and the baby is safely delivered, however, the mother is maimed and dies of her injuries.\n\nThe family sues. The doctors pay. Governments and medical associations increase the R&D funding to improve the design. Corporations go back to work. Insurance companies continue to cover the doctors but only if they\'re part of a government-backed hospital.\n\nBack at the drawing board, they redesign the machine to do the job more slowly, and develop medications to help the mother adapt to the new process.\n\nThe birth is successful, but the medications affect the baby with a lifelong disability, and the mother\'s guts herniate the first time she stands up. Life-long treatment for both mother and child is covered now by government programmed insurance, because the insurance companies can no longer afford to cover the program, even though the doctors, scientists, engineers, politicians and corporations ALL declare that the new process is "safe and effective."\n\nAlong comes a man that says, "Hey, the new process is far more dangerous than natural childbirth. Why don\'t we go back to that?"\n\nPoliticians, doctors, lawyers, insurance companies, scientists and engineers (who all make HUGE amounts of money on the new process) call the man a "conspiracy theorist" a "science denier" and a slew of other epithets to tarnish his name.\n\nNone of the accusations change the fact that a Lamaze class and natural childbirth are safer than the "new process."\n\nIn this case the man is @RobertKennedyJr and the above interested parties (not including the families) are having the same reaction to the potential loss equaling about $5 TRILLION in stupid ideas.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '337808606', 'name': 'Robert F. Kennedy Jr', 'screen_name': 'RobertKennedyJr', 'indices': [2502, 2518]}]}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 3, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Wed Jan 29 18:07:38 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1884645057766064619', 'display_text_range': [31, 304], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}, {'id_str': '337808606', 'name': 'Robert F. Kennedy Jr', 'screen_name': 'RobertKennedyJr', 'indices': [14, 30]}]}, 'favorite_count': 21, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': "@TheChiefNerd @RobertKennedyJr I have an analogy for you. Please bear with me.\n\n